Design LFU Cache

(LFU = Least Frequently Used)

🟢 Problem Statement

Design a data structure that supports:

LFUCache(int capacity)
int get(int key)
void put(int key, int value)

Rules:

If key exists → return value

If not → return -1

When capacity is full:

Remove the least frequently used key

If multiple keys have same frequency:

Remove the least recently used among them

⚡ All operations must be O(1)

🟢 Example
Input:
capacity = 2

put(1,1)
put(2,2)
get(1) → 1
put(3,3)
get(2) → -1
get(3) → 3
put(4,4)
get(1) → -1
get(3) → 3
get(4) → 4

🟢 Why This Is Hard

LRU only cares about recency.

LFU cares about:
1️⃣ Frequency
2️⃣ Recency inside same frequency

So we need double level ordering.

🟢 Core Idea

We maintain:

1️⃣ HashMap → key → Node
2️⃣ HashMap → frequency → DoublyLinkedList
3️⃣ Minimum frequency tracker
🟢 Data Structures
keyMap        : Map<key, Node>
freqMap       : Map<frequency, DoublyLinkedList>
minFrequency  : int

🟢 Node Structure

Each node contains:

key
value
frequency
prev
next

🟢 Algorithm
get(key)

If not present → return -1

Increase frequency

Move node to next frequency list

Update minFrequency if needed

put(key, value)

If capacity == 0 → return

If key exists:

Update value

Call get(key) to update frequency

Else:

If full → remove node from minFrequency list

Insert new node with frequency 1

minFrequency = 1

🟢 Java Implementation (Interview Level)
import java.util.*;

class LFUCache {

    class Node {
        int key, value, freq;
        Node prev, next;

        Node(int k, int v) {
            key = k;
            value = v;
            freq = 1;
        }
    }

    class DoublyLinkedList {
        Node head, tail;
        int size;

        DoublyLinkedList() {
            head = new Node(0,0);
            tail = new Node(0,0);
            head.next = tail;
            tail.prev = head;
            size = 0;
        }

        void add(Node node) {
            node.next = head.next;
            node.prev = head;
            head.next.prev = node;
            head.next = node;
            size++;
        }

        void remove(Node node) {
            node.prev.next = node.next;
            node.next.prev = node.prev;
            size--;
        }

        Node removeLast() {
            if(size > 0) {
                Node node = tail.prev;
                remove(node);
                return node;
            }
            return null;
        }
    }

    int capacity, minFreq;
    Map<Integer, Node> keyMap;
    Map<Integer, DoublyLinkedList> freqMap;

    public LFUCache(int capacity) {
        this.capacity = capacity;
        minFreq = 0;
        keyMap = new HashMap<>();
        freqMap = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public int get(int key) {

        if(!keyMap.containsKey(key))
            return -1;

        Node node = keyMap.get(key);
        updateFrequency(node);
        return node.value;
    }

    public void put(int key, int value) {

        if(capacity == 0)
            return;

        if(keyMap.containsKey(key)) {

            Node node = keyMap.get(key);
            node.value = value;
            updateFrequency(node);

        } else {

            if(keyMap.size() == capacity) {

                DoublyLinkedList minList = freqMap.get(minFreq);
                Node removed = minList.removeLast();
                keyMap.remove(removed.key);
            }

            Node newNode = new Node(key, value);
            keyMap.put(key, newNode);

            freqMap.putIfAbsent(1, new DoublyLinkedList());
            freqMap.get(1).add(newNode);

            minFreq = 1;
        }
    }

    private void updateFrequency(Node node) {

        int oldFreq = node.freq;
        DoublyLinkedList oldList = freqMap.get(oldFreq);
        oldList.remove(node);

        if(oldFreq == minFreq && oldList.size == 0)
            minFreq++;

        node.freq++;

        freqMap.putIfAbsent(node.freq, new DoublyLinkedList());
        freqMap.get(node.freq).add(node);
    }
}

🟢 Step-by-Step Explanation
Node
int key, value, freq;


Each key tracks its frequency.

DoublyLinkedList

Used to maintain LRU inside same frequency.

Important functions:

add(node)
remove(node)
removeLast()


RemoveLast → least recently used

🟢 get(key)
updateFrequency(node);


We:

Remove node from current freq list

Increase freq

Add to new freq list

🟢 put(key, value)

Case 1: Key exists
→ Update value
→ Increase frequency

Case 2: New key

If full:

freqMap.get(minFreq).removeLast()


Remove least frequent + least recently used

Insert new key with freq = 1

